From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000016
Subject: [PATCH] @companion honours the population master switch

With population_engine_enable: 0 the engine loads none of its databases, but @companion still
ran: it listed, summoned and drafted companions, and changed their saved rows. Refuse it the
way 0002 refuses @populate, before any subcommand, so a disabled engine reads and writes no
companion row and turning it back on finds every companion as it was. The companion window
asks through "@companion list raw", so it shows nothing while the engine is off.

--- a/src/custom/atcommand.inc
+++ b/src/custom/atcommand.inc
@@ -275,6 +275,12 @@
 ACMD_FUNC(companion)
 {
 	nullpo_retr(-1, sd);
+	// The population master switch covers companions too: with it off nothing here runs and no
+	// saved companion is read or changed, so turning it back on brings them all back as they were.
+	if (!battle_config.population_engine_enable) {
+		clif_displaymessage(fd, "The population engine is disabled. Turn it on in the app's settings.");
+		return -1;
+	}
 	// RAGNAROKMAC: room for a full 23-character name AND what follows it ("homunculus <name> off",
 	// "skills <name> toggle <id>", "gear <name> weapon shield"). A NAME_LENGTH buffer cut those
 	// off after the name, so the trailing word was silently dropped. Names are still bounded to
